   554	/**
   555	 * idn2_to_ascii_4i:
   556	 * @input: zero terminated input Unicode (UCS-4) string.
   557	 * @inlen: number of elements in @input.
   558	 * @output: output zero terminated string that must have room for at least 63 characters plus the terminating zero.
   559	 * @flags: optional #idn2_flags to modify behaviour.
   560	 *
   561	 * THIS FUNCTION HAS BEEN DEPRECATED DUE TO A DESIGN FLAW. USE idn2_to_ascii_4i2() INSTEAD !
   562	 *
   563	 * The ToASCII operation takes a sequence of Unicode code points that make
   564	 * up one domain label and transforms it into a sequence of code points in
   565	 * the ASCII range (0..7F). If ToASCII succeeds, the original sequence and
   566	 * the resulting sequence are equivalent labels.
   567	 *
   568	 * It is important to note that the ToASCII operation can fail.
   569	 * ToASCII fails if any step of it fails. If any step of the
   570	 * ToASCII operation fails on any label in a domain name, that domain
   571	 * name MUST NOT be used as an internationalized domain name.
   572	 * The method for dealing with this failure is application-specific.
   573	 *
   574	 * The inputs to ToASCII are a sequence of code points.
   575	 *
   576	 * ToASCII never alters a sequence of code points that are all in the ASCII
   577	 * range to begin with (although it could fail). Applying the ToASCII operation multiple
   578	 * effect as applying it just once.
   579	 *
   580	 * The default behavior of this function (when flags are zero) is to apply
   581	 * the IDNA2008 rules without the TR46 amendments. As the TR46
